Usage: agent-deck session restart [id|title] [options]

Restart a session. For Claude sessions, this reloads MCPs.

By default, a restart is skipped (no-op) when the session is already
healthy (running/waiting/idle/starting) and was started within the last
60 seconds. This prevents watchdog double-fires from destroying a
just-created tmux scope (issue #30). Use --force to restart anyway.

A restart is also skipped when the session's agent could not authenticate
(401 / invalid credentials): a restart cannot fix a credential, and each
attempt races the rotating token shared by every session on this host.
Re-authenticate (run /login), then restart — --force overrides the hold.

--all paces restarts with a jittered stagger, caps how many un-verified
boots run at once, skips auth-held sessions, and STOPS early if several
restarts in a row die on authentication (reported as auth_tripped).

Options:

Examples:
  agent-deck session restart my-project
  agent-deck session restart my-project --env API_URL=https://api.example.com
  agent-deck session restart my-project --env FOO=one --env BAR=two
  agent-deck session restart --all
